ಮೊದಲು:
==Kannada==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|kn|dra-pro|*mutal||first, beginning}}. Cognate with {{cog|ta|முதல்}}, {{cog|te|మొదలు}}, {{cog|ml|മുതൽ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{kn-IPA|ಮೊದಲು}}

===Adverb===
{{kn-adv}}
# [[first]], [[beforehand]]
#: {{ux|kn|ಅವನು ಮೊದಲು ಬಂದನು.|tr=Avanu modalu bandanu.|t=He came first.}}
# [[before]], [[ago]]
#: {{ux|kn|ಕೆಲಸದ ಮೊದಲು ಸ್ವಲ್ಪ ವಿಶ್ರಾಂತಿ ಪಡೆಯಿರಿ.|tr=Kelasada modalu swalpa viśrānti paḍeyiri.|t=Take some rest before the work.}}

===Noun===
# [[beginning]], [[start]]
#: {{ux|kn|ಅವಳು ಮೊದಲಿನಿಂದ ಪ್ರಾರಂಭಿಸಿದಳು.|tr=Avaḷu modalininda prāraṃbhisidaḷu.|t=She started from the beginning.}}

====Declension====
{{kn-decl-u|ಮೊದಲು| ಮೊದಲ}}

===Usage notes===
* While {{m|kn|ಮೊದಲು}} can mean "beginning," it primarily refers to **sequence** or **priority** (what comes "first" in time or order).
* For the **formal act of starting** a project, a journey, or an era, {{m|kn|ಆರಂಭ}} or {{m|kn|ಪ್ರಾರಂಭ}} is more natural. 
* **Example:** Use {{m|kn|ಮೊದಲು}} for "finish this first," but use {{m|kn|ಪ್ರಾರಂಭ}} for "the start of the meeting".

====Derived terms====
* {{l|kn|ಮೊದಲ|tr=modala|t=first}}

===References===
* {{R:kn:Alar}}

